PROJECT GOAL: We aim to verify if the user needs to set up a build environment to resolve the issue:

1. Does not need build environment
   (The solutions/answers can be validated without build environment, e.g., it's a conceptual issue, documentation issue, or can be verified with simple code analysis)

2. Can be dockerized without any issue
   (The solutions must require a build environment to be verified)

3. Requires build environment but hard to be dockerized or cannot be reproduced now
   (The solution must require a build environment, but it is difficult to containerize for reasons such as: hardware dependencies, network dependencies, external API access with authentication, timing-dependent behaviors, requiring MacOS, multiple users interacting simultaneously, licensed software, etc.)

IMPORTANT GUIDELINES:
- Choose category 1 whenever possible. If the LLM can analyze the issue and verify the solution without needing to build or run the code, always select category 1.
- Only classify an issue as requiring a build environment (categories 2 or 3) when it's ABSOLUTELY NECESSARY to actually build and run the code to verify if the solution works.

GitHub Issue:
Post Date: 2018-01-12T18:16:25Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Failure sending multiple simultaneous emails
Description: After upgrading our solution from MailKit 1.x version to 2.0.1 version, we have started to experience errors whenever we attempt to send e-mails on multiple threads at the same time.

We receive one of the two following errors:

> Error reading a response from the SMTP server. => Cannot access a disposed object.
> Object name: 'SslStream'.

> Error reading a response from the SMTP server. =>  The BeginRead method cannot be called when another read operation is pending.

Is there any reference on how to properly use new asynchronous APIs?

This is code sample from our app:

    public class MailerProcess
    {
        public static void Run()
        {
             using (SmtpClient client = new SmtpClient())
             {
                   string host = AppSettingsWrapper.Host;
                   string port = AppSettingsWrapper.Port.ToString();

                   client.Connect(AppSettingsWrapper.Host, AppSettingsWrapper.Port, SecureSocketOptions.Auto);
                   client.Authenticate(AppSettingsWrapper.UserName, AppSettingsWrapper.Password);
                   client.Timeout = AppSettingsWrapper.Timeout;

 	           List<Task> taskList = new List<Task>();
 
                   foreach (MailerJob job in batch)
                   {
                        taskList.Add(SendAsync(client, fm, job.Email));
                   }

                   Task.WhenAll(taskList).Wait();

                   if(client.IsConnected)
                   {
                        client.Disconnect(true);
                   }
              }
        }

        private static async Task SendAsync(SmtpClient client, IFileManager fm, Email email)
        {
            try
            {
                MimeMessage message = new MimeMessage();

                MailboxAddress from = new MailboxAddress(email.Content.FromDisplayName, email.Content.FromAddress);
                MailboxAddress to = new MailboxAddress(email.Content.ToDisplayName, email.Content.ToAddress);
                message.From.Add(from);
                message.To.Add(to);

                message.Subject = email.Content.Subject;

                BodyBuilder bodyBuilder = new BodyBuilder();
                if (email.Content.IsHtmlContent)
                {
                    bodyBuilder.HtmlBody = email.Content.Body;
                }
                else
                {
                    bodyBuilder.TextBody = email.Content.Body;
                }

                message.Body = bodyBuilder.ToMessageBody();

                if (client.IsConnected)
                {
                    await client.SendAsync(message);
                }
                return;
            }
            catch (SmtpCommandException se)
            {
                email.StatusMessage = se.Message;
                email.StatusCode = (int)se.StatusCode;
            }
            catch (Exception e)
            {
                email.StatusMessage = e.RecursiveMessage();
            }
        }
    }

Run method is invoked from .NET Core 2.0 console application.


